Track 3: Spun Cullet Swallows the Bogie
- Story & Context: Legend spread along the line that during the historic cold wave of December 2017, an entire sleeper car synced their gear through contact mics pressed against the carriage's frost-crystallized window panes, matching the half-time sway of a freight train transporting raw molten cullet to the Firozabad furnaces. When the conductor opened the compartment door at 4:00 AM to demand travel passes, he was greeted by eighteen passengers swaying in total silence beneath woolen shawls, murmuring "We bought no tickets but the rails knew our names" while the double bass vibrated the floorboards with hypnotic, rhythmic sub-frequencies. The conductor quietly stepped back into the corridor, turned off the carriage fluorescent lights, and left them to ride uninterrupted to the end of the line.
